        "url": "https://x.com/jwt0625/status/2067488692026175689",
        "tweets": [
            {
                "text": "can confirm I can see the veins on my hand and the bones in my arm with their smaller scale table top demo, in semi realtime.\nthe arrays are synchronized but not to the coherent degree yet, but nothing stopping the whole thing from being coherent soon, which means it can revert the measured scattering, and create all kinds of fields like acoustic tweezers in your body and e.g. move stuff around lol\nI'm the most jealous on how easy it is to make such a big phased array for ultrasound compared to optical phased array, not to mention an array of an array..\nit's still hard, it's just a bit easier than with light, it took 20 years from Prof. Khuri-Yakub's 1998 paper on CMUT to the commercial launch of Butterfly iQ in 2018.\n( pictures are for one array, from Butterfly Network folks' ISSCC 2021 paper )",
                "media": [
                    {
                        "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HLEwjt2a4AAG00Y?format=jpg",
                        "local_path": "media/20260618_014324_0.jpg"
                    },
                    {
                        "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HLEwsb0a0AAsoON?format=jpg",
                        "local_path": "media/20260618_014324_1.jpg"
                    },
                    {
