    {
        "url": "https://x.com/jwt0625/status/2068192042229068170",
        "tweets": [
            {
                "text": "if you run some simple estimations, you'll find regardless of whatever optical engines you use, the scale-up among multiple racks will need thousands to tens of thousands of optical fibers running in and out of each rack.\n(\nhttps://x.com/jwt0625/status/2065464510501286060)\nHow are you going to splice, protect, connect, and manage this many fibers? The astronomers have kind of done it, and they are absolutely pushing the frontiers of more extreme fiber systems.\nSome of the connector vendors have worked on fiber optic connectors for 20+ years, I really want to get into their heads..\nOfc the telecom industry have also have many amazing cables and cable management, but they no longer tell you as much.",
                "media": [
                    {
                        "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HLOwzUWakAAG4Ru?format=jpg",
                        "local_path": "media/20260612_160128_0.jpg"
                    },
                    {
                        "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HLOxcmLbgAIVR9f?format=jpg",
                        "local_path": "media/20260612_160128_1.jpg"
                    },
                    {
                        "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKoAhSwbsAAtikc?format=jpg",
                        "local_path": "media/20260612_160128_2.jpg"
                    }
                ],
                "timestamp": "2026-06-12T16:01:28+00:00"
            },
            {
                "text": "their splicing station reminds me of multi chamber tools from amat lol. Also so rare to see a detailed analysis of negative aspects.\n- Poppett2024: [Overview of the Fiber System for the Dark Energy Spectroscopic Instrument](\nhttp://doi.org/10.3847/1538-3881/ad76a4)",
                "media": [
                    {
                        "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HLOyb2FbYAA9IEt?format=jpg",
                        "local_path": "media/20260620_045035_0.jpg"
                    },
                    {
                        "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HLOzBohaEAA5myu?format=jpg",
                        "local_path": "media/20260620_045035_1.jpg"
                    },
                    {
                        "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HLOz3Y1bsAE1Ll1?format=jpg",
                        "local_path": "media/20260620_045035_2.jpg"
                    },
                    {
                        "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HLOz-qeagAAWEmX?format=png",
                        "local_path": "media/20260620_045035_3.jpg"
                    }
                ],
                "timestamp": "2026-06-20T04:50:35+00:00"
            },
            {
                "text": "like why do you need this much crap to plug in a connector? This is amazing.\n[Kit MMC-16, Female, Single-Mode, MMC Elite, Green Housing, Jacket Crimp, 28mm Boot](\nhttps://www.usconec.com/umbraco/rhythm/protectedfilesapi/download?path=%2ffiles%2fdrawings%2fC25519.pdf)",
                "media": [
                    {
                        "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HLO1DlobMAECcta?format=jpg",
                        "local_path": "media/20260620_045528_0.jpg"
                    }
                ],
                "timestamp": "2026-06-20T04:55:28+00:00"
            },
            {
                "text": "the 5000 fiber vesion was all spliced, they want connectorized because there will be 20k+ fibers, and they want silica ferrule instead of polymer ferrule, for more consistent connector stability and repeatability.\nGalal2026: [Ultra-precise Multi-fiber Optical Connectors for Astronomy](\nhttps://arxiv.org/abs/2606.19043)",
                "media": [
                    {
                        "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HLO1hbsa4AAchpy?format=jpg",
                        "local_path": "media/20260620_050131_0.jpg"
                    },
                    {
                        "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HLO1oKZasAANnSR?format=jpg",
