    {
        "url": "https://x.com/jwt0625/status/2069442540752003209",
        "tweets": [
            {
                "text": "people usually use multimode fiber (MMF, OM3 and OM4 etc) with ~850 nm VCSELs. At 1060 nm you need custom MMF, or a ~1 um wavelength single mode fiber (SMF-28 for 1.5 um is multimode here).\nguess what the insertion loss is between the 1060 nm VCSEL and the SMF?",
                "media": [
                    {
                        "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HLgh5q_a8AAxdB6?format=png",
                        "local_path": "media/20260623_152844_0.jpg"
                    }
                ],
                "timestamp": "2026-06-23T15:28:44+00:00"
            },
            {
                "text": "about 1 dB, pretty damn decent, probably better than COUPE's grating couplers. They sent 8x100G PAM4 over 2 km with this VCSEL + SMF. From Furukawa and FUJIFILM.\n- Yoshida2026: [A 106-Gb/s × 8-Channel 1060-nm Single-Mode VCSEL-Based Ultra-Compact CPO Transceiver enabling 2-km Parallel-Optical Links](\nhttps://doi.org/10.1109/ECTC51846.2026.00020)",
                "media": [
                    {
                        "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HLgjJD3a4AEsg4C?format=jpg",
                        "local_path": "media/20260623_153134_0.jpg"
                    },
                    {
                        "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HLgjLn8a0AAQK8E?format=jpg",
                        "local_path": "media/20260623_153134_1.jpg"
                    }
                ],
                "timestamp": "2026-06-23T15:31:34+00:00"
            }
        ]
